  "details": "As of right now, you are able to override avatar culling to always show avatars of friends and of those who you manually showed.\n\nI would love for these features to be implemented into the earmuff feature. I have been in worlds many times that are crowded, and I turn around for a second and then I am unable to hear my friends due to earmuffs. I do not want to increase the range of earmuffs or turn them off because I don't want to hear 20 loud people, yet I still want to hear my friends. With a setting to \"override earmuffs\", maybe attached to show avatar or as another \"moderation\" action, and a \"override for friends\" by default setting I think this could help a lot of people who go to crowded public instances, such as clubs and other events.\n\n(I did not see a option for this in game nor a feature request for this, so if there already is my bad)",
